From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:26:59 -0400
Subject: libclammspack: Validate LZX match offsets before narrowing (#144)

The LZX decoder narrows an unsigned wrapped-window distance to int
before checking it against the window size. Crafted repeated offsets
can narrow to a negative value, bypass the check, and cause an
out-of-bounds copy.

Check the unsigned distance first, then cast only a value bounded by
the window size.

Reported by Feng Xue and XGPT of ThreatBook.

CLAM-3085

---
Upstream: https://github.com/Cisco-Talos/clamav/commit/eb4490921668724378b6284458fc9737746468a5
CVE: CVE-2026-76421
Signed-off-by: Titouan Christophe <titouan.christophe@mind.be>
---
 libclammspack/mspack/lzxd.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libclammspack/mspack/lzxd.c b/libclammspack/mspack/lzxd.c
index f498dba95e..fa37f5339d 100644
--- a/libclammspack/mspack/lzxd.c
+++ b/libclammspack/mspack/lzxd.c
@@ -627,11 +627,11 @@ int lzxd_decompress(struct lzxd_stream *lzx, off_t out_bytes) {
                 return lzx->error = MSPACK_ERR_DECRUNCH;
               }
               /* j = length from match offset to end of window */
-              j = match_offset - window_posn;
-              if (j > (int) lzx->window_size) {
+              if ((match_offset - window_posn) > lzx->window_size) {
                 D(("match offset beyond window boundaries"))
                 return lzx->error = MSPACK_ERR_DECRUNCH;
               }
+              j = (int) (match_offset - window_posn);
               runsrc = &window[lzx->window_size - j];
               if (j < i) {
                 /* if match goes over the window edge, do two copy runs */
